          "id": "5047f47ac76dbd0d66ccceb0b5945310ba161ae3",
          "message": "GH_ISSUE_927: hoist per-cycle telemetry out of business logic (#937)\n\nTwo targeted refactors:\n\noverreplication.clean now defers a single reportCleanCycle that owns\nevery per-cycle metric (RunsTotal status label, Duration histogram,\nPending gauge reset, RemovedTotal counter) and the completion audit\nlog. The body of clean reads as straight cleanup work; every exit\npath reports through one place instead of repeating the telemetry\ntriplet three different ways.\n\nprobeDestAfterAmbiguousCopy lifts its repeated log-attribute set\n(source_key, dest_key, backend, copy_error) into a shared base slice,\nthen switches on the three outcomes (HEAD failed / size mismatch /\nrecovered). Same logs, no field duplication.\n\nThe other three audit candidates (maybeWrapIntegrityReader,\nProcessPendingQueue, PutObject failover loop) turned out to already\nbe in the outcome-pattern shape the issue describes. No change to\nthose.\n\nNo behaviour change. Tests pass under -race.",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-23T23:25:23Z",
